M3.9 final read-only health diagnosis
Date: 2026-08-28
Result: privileged invocation unavailable; runtime unchanged

The final read-only check attempted to execute the versioned health command as
the dedicated runtime identity through non-interactive sudo. The server
correctly rejected that privilege transition because an interactive password
would be required. No password was requested, no privilege or sudo policy was
changed, and the service remained enabled, active and unchanged.

The acceptance continues only with unprivileged read-only checks available to
the chatops identity. Any failure to obtain a fresh safe health result through
those existing rights remains fail-closed and must not be represented as GO.

The same health command under the unprivileged chatops identity returned the
safe `RED` envelope because that identity cannot read the runtime-owned 0600
status file. This is an observation-permission failure, not evidence that the
runtime changed state. The final report therefore distinguishes the last
privileged READY acceptance from the later unprivileged service observations.
